\section{Étale coverings of a normal scheme}
\label{I.10}

\begin{proposition}
\label{I.10.1}
Let \(X\) be a prescheme that is étale and separated over a connected normal
prescheme~\(Y\) with function field~\(K\). Then the connected components
\(X_i\) of~\(X\) are integral, their function fields \(K_i\) are finite
separable extensions of~\(K\), and each \(X_i\) is identified with a nonempty
open subset of the normalization of~\(X\) in~\(K_i\) (and hence \(X\) is
identified with a dense open subset of the normalization
of~\(Y\) in \(R(X)=L=\prod K_i\)).
\end{proposition}

\paragraph{Editorial note.}
The corrected French authority TeX, the original printing, and the corrected
re-typeset witness all read \(X\) in the first normalization clause, and the
proof repeats \(X\). The parenthetical conclusion and the Main Theorem
argument appear to require \(Y\). We retain the attested reading and flag the
apparent source oddity.
